{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3AlgebraInstance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3AlgebraInstance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3AlgebraLaws","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Pi"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H3A.markovTrace_H3A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H3A.markovTrace_H3A","kind":"instance","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraInstance.lean#L117-L126","doc":"**The FIRST instance of the `MarkovTrace` class** — the concrete n=3\nMarkov trace on `H3A R h` satisfies every class field: (M2) cyclicity from\n`trM_cyclic`, (M1a) additivity from `trM_add`, (M1b) homogeneity from\n`trM_smul`. The interface's \"eventual instance\" now exists, with real\ncontent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H3A.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H3A.trace","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraInstance.lean#L114-L115","doc":"The Markov trace on the wrapper, at Markov parameter `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H3A.instAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H3A.instAlgebra","kind":"instance","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraInstance.lean#L107-L112","doc":"**The H₃(q) NF module is an `R`-algebra** — scalar action compatible\nwith `mulNF` on both sides (the proved homogeneity laws). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H3A.instRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H3A